Subject: [PATCH] t2bce: limit the shared-link DMA gate to hibernation

Patch 0005 registered t2bce_suspend_noirq()/t2bce_resume_noirq() as the
ordinary .suspend_noirq/.resume_noirq callbacks and routed .resume through
t2bce_resume_with_shared_dma().  The verify step in t2bce_resume_noirq()
(fail with -EIO and latch pci_dma_restore_failed when any of the four 74:00.x
functions has PCI_COMMAND bus-master set) only makes sense for hibernation,
where DMA must stay blocked until the restored kernel rebuilds its state.
After a real ACPI S3 wake firmware leaves bus-master set on the sibling
functions (function 2 is the unbound SEP function), so every S3 resume failed:

  t2bce_core: noirq: blocked shared-link DMA and saved disabled state mask=0x6
  t2bce_core: noirq: shared-link DMA became enabled during restore
  t2bce_core 0000:74:00.1: PM: failed to resume noirq: error -5

Remove .suspend_noirq/.resume_noirq and use the plain t2bce_resume() for
.resume so ordinary S3 takes the pre-0005 path: no noirq DMA gate, no latch
consultation, and no bus-master clearing after a failed resume.  The
hibernation mappings (.freeze_noirq, .thaw_noirq, .poweroff_noirq,
.restore_noirq, .thaw, .restore) are unchanged, and .freeze_noirq still
resets the latch and saved mask at the start of every hibernation transition.
.resume is never invoked by the hibernation phases, so the latch is
unreachable on S3.

This is an unqualified source-only change; it has not been built, staged or
tested on hardware.

---
diff --git a/drivers/staging/t2bce/t2bce_core/t2bce_main.c b/drivers/staging/t2bce/t2bce_core/t2bce_main.c
--- a/drivers/staging/t2bce/t2bce_core/t2bce_main.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/t2bce/t2bce_core/t2bce_main.c
@@ -1137,9 +1137,10 @@
 struct dev_pm_ops t2bce_pci_driver_pm = {
         .prepare = t2bce_prepare,
         .suspend = t2bce_suspend,
-        .resume = t2bce_resume_with_shared_dma,
-        .suspend_noirq = t2bce_suspend_noirq,
-        .resume_noirq = t2bce_resume_noirq,
+        /* Ordinary S3 uses the plain BCE resume and no noirq DMA gate; the
+         * shared-link block is hibernation-only (freeze/poweroff/thaw/restore).
+         */
+        .resume = t2bce_resume,
         .freeze = t2bce_freeze,
         .thaw = t2bce_resume_with_shared_dma,
         .poweroff = t2bce_freeze,
